 "caption_summary": "From an OCT volume to I-JEPA pretraining and volume-level evaluation. (a) Each FairVision volume has 200 B-scans; pretraining and evaluation use the same 100 evenly spaced ones, resized to 256 by 256 pixels (N=256 patches of 16 by 16 pixels). (b) Each B-scan is a separate sample (random resized crop). Strategies differ in the sampler of context C (grey: omitted tokens) and targets T_m (uniform or from A_s(x); CENTROID's masks of Figure 1); encoders, predictor and loss are shared. The predictor sees h_C and mask tokens at the target positions; the EMA target encoder's normalized outputs at T_m are the stop-gradient Smooth-L1 targets. (c) The frozen EMA encoder sees uncropped B-scans; patch features are averaged per B-scan, then across the volume, before a LayerNorm-linear head. Stacks are schematic; the B-scan is the OCTDL crop.",
 "alt_text": "Three panels. (a) A schematic stack of OCT B-scans with alternate slices marked used, an example B-scan with a 16 by 16 patch grid. (b) I-JEPA: view x and guide feed a sampler; the context view goes through the context encoder and predictor with mask tokens at the target positions (numbered tokens 1 to 4 in the group colours); the full view goes through the EMA target encoder, LayerNorm and target selection with stop-gradient; Smooth-L1 per target group. (c) The frozen EMA encoder encodes each of 100 B-scans; patch tokens are averaged per B-scan, B-scan vectors averaged per volume, then LayerNorm and linear head give the glaucoma probability.",
